<statement>
<p>Solve the triangle</p><image width="58%" pi:generated="problems/images/mom-835746-1.png"/>
<p><m>\displaystyle\angle{B}</m> is <fillin characters="5"/>    degrees
  </p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{a}=</m> <fillin characters="5"/>   
  </p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{c}=</m> <fillin characters="5"/>   
</p>
<p>Round to 2 decimal places.</p>


</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li>63</li><li>8.42</li><li>11.87</li></ul></p>
</answer>
<solution><p>We want to know the length of a side opposite a known angle. The law of sines could help. However, we do not yet know the angle across from the known side.</p>
<p>We calculate that using the known measures of the other two angles. <m>\displaystyle{180}^{\circ}-{43}^{\circ}-{74}^{\circ}={63}^{\circ}</m>.</p>
<p>Now we can use law of sines to calculate the desired side length.</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle\frac{{\sin{{\left({43}^{\circ}\right)}}}}{{a}}=\frac{{\sin{{\left({63}^{\circ}\right)}}}}{{11}}</m>.</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{11}{\sin{{\left({43}^{\circ}\right)}}}={a}{\sin{{\left({63}^{\circ}\right)}}}</m>.</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{11}\frac{{\sin{{\left({43}^{\circ}\right)}}}}{{\sin{{\left({63}^{\circ}\right)}}}}={a}</m>.</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{8.4196711887392}={a}</m></p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{8.42}\approx{a}</m></p>
<p><m>\displaystyle\frac{{\sin{{\left({74}^{\circ}\right)}}}}{{c}}=\frac{{\sin{{\left({63}^{\circ}\right)}}}}{{11}}</m>.</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{11}{\sin{{\left({74}^{\circ}\right)}}}={c}{\sin{{\left({63}^{\circ}\right)}}}</m>.</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{11}\frac{{\sin{{\left({74}^{\circ}\right)}}}}{{\sin{{\left({63}^{\circ}\right)}}}}={c}</m>.</p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{11.867341448429}={c}</m></p>
<p>
  <m>\displaystyle{11.87}\approx{c}</m></p></solution>
</myopenmath>